jobs.description:
Our client is an international fashion and apparel company with a strong presence across European markets. The Finance team is looking for additional support due to a temporary increase in workload and the upcoming annual budgeting cycle.

Jobomschrijving

As a Freelance Business Controller your responsibilities are:

• Support month-end and year-end closing, including reconciliations and consolidation ;
• Analyse revenue, margins, stocks and performance variances versus budget and previous years ;
• Support the preparation of annual budgets, forecasts and financial models ;
• Prepare management and Board reporting, presentations and ad hoc financial analyses ;
• Support cash flow forecasting and financial planning ;
• Act as a business partner to commercial and operational teams ;
• Challenge assumptions and contribute to business cases and investment decisions ;
• Improve and automate controlling processes, reporting and financial tools ;

A successful Freelance Business Controller should have:

• University degree in Finance, Economics, Business or a related field ;
• Minimum 3 years of experience in Business Controlling or Financial Analysis ;
• Strong understanding of controlling, accounting principles and financial reporting ;
• Experience with budgeting, forecasting and financial modelling ;
• Strong analytical skills with excellent Excel knowledge; BI experience is a plus ;
• Interest in digitalisation, data tools and business systems ;
• Structured, proactive and hands-on with strong attention to detail ;
• Fluent in French and English ;

As an F&B Waiter/Waitress - Bartender, you will attend to guests in the restaurant, room service, bar and banqueting areas, ensuring professional and efficient service in line with the hotel's standards.

Your main responsibilities include:
- welcoming and seating guests upon arrival;
- assisting guests in choosing food and beverages and providing information about menu items;
- taking accurate food and beverage orders and entering them into the POS system;
- preparing the necessary accompaniments and equipment for service;
- serving food and beverages according to service standards;
- responding to additional guest requests and ensuring their comfort and satisfaction;
- maintaining a professional, prompt and friendly service at all times;
- ensuring tables are properly set with the required cutlery, glassware, linen and equipment;
- maintaining a good knowledge of menu and beverage items;
- keeping tables, chairs, service stations, bar areas and equipment clean and properly organised;
- clearing tables and collecting used dishes, glassware, linen and room-service trays;
- preparing sufficient service equipment to ensure efficient service;
- carrying out daily and weekly cleaning duties and other operational tasks when required;
- maintaining food and beverage displays and ensuring that service areas remain tidy and presentable;
- handling the assigned cash float and collecting payments for products and services;
- ensuring that consumptions are posted correctly and on time;
- reporting problems, unusual situations or special guest requests promptly to the supervisor;
- carrying out reasonable requests from the manager, supervisor or management team.
This list of responsibilities is not exhaustive.

- First professional experience required.
- Good command of French and English.
- Strong customer-service orientation.
- Ability to provide friendly, efficient and professional service.
- Attention to cleanliness, presentation and service standards.

- Contract: fixed-term or permanent contract (CDD/CDI)
- Working schedule: full-time
